{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1834 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "205174d608fef374a2eefb94d1af0999701b611fb2b3bcbe562069587663ab97" :edb/db-before-t 1833 :edb/db-after-t 1834 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535146 50 #inst "2026-10-08T17:58:25.881Z" 13194139535146 true] [17592186124371 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333783 13194139535146 true] [17592186124371 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333804 13194139535146 true] [17592186124375 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333811 13194139535146 true] [17592186124479 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333790 13194139535146 true] [17592186124479 1020 #edb/ref 17592186333797 13194139535146 true] [17592186333783 1017 #edb/ref 17592186333784 13194139535146 true] [17592186333783 1089 "q-129339" 13194139535146 true] [17592186333783 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535146 true] [17592186333783 1100 "Find ${lim}_{x\\to (-1,-1)}\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}-xy}.$" 13194139535146 true] [17592186333783 1113 #uuid "750bd076-cd76-5f0d-b037-66703830aec4" 13194139535146 true] [17592186333783 1145 "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1,-1)}\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}-xy} & =\\frac{(-1)^{2}-(-1)^{2}}{(-1)^{2}-(-1)(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-1}{1-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1,-1)}\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}-xy} & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1,-1)}\\frac{(x+y)(x-y)}{x(x-y)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1,-1)}\\frac{(x+y)\\cancel{(x-y)}}{x\\cancel{(x-y)}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1,-1)}\\frac{x+y}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it using direct substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1,-1)}\\frac{x+y}{x} & =\\frac{-1+(-1)}{(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)}{(-1)} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $2.$" 13194139535146 true] [17592186333784 1000 #