g to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}+x-y}{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{0}-\\sqrt{0}+0-0}{\\sqrt{0}-\\sqrt{0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-0+0-0}{0-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by first multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}+x-y}{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}} & ={lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}+x-y)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})}{(\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y})(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y})(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})+(x-y)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})}{x-y} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{x-y+(x-y)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})}{x-y} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{(x-y)(1+\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})}{x-y} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{\\cancel{(x-y)}(1+\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})}{\\cancel{x-y}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}(1+\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}(1+\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y}) & =1+\\sqrt{0}+\\sqrt{0} \\\\  & =1+0+0 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $1.$" 13194139535146 true] [17592186333791 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333792 13194139535146 true] [17592186333791 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333793 13194139535146 true] [17592186333791 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333794 13194139535146 true] [17592186333791 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333795 13194139535146 true] [17592186333791 1000 #edb/ref 17592186333796 13194139535146 true] [17592186333791 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535146 true] [17592186333791 1041 "selection" 13194139535146 true] [17592186333791 1104 #edb/ref 17592186333795 13194139535146 true] [17592186333791 1110 #uuid "c5adf6ff-a8bb-53c5-ac42-8f3743f775b1" 13194139535146 true] [17592186333792 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535146 